47
00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.960
Once the sprint is actually running, you need tools to monitor its health.

48
00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.900
Think of the burndown chart like an EKG monitor for your team.

49
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.800
And this brilliantly illustrates how reading the shape of that chart

50
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.920
helps PMs identify bottlenecks super early.

51
00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.360
If the line has an ideal, steady downward slope, your pacing is smooth.

52
00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.040
You're golden.

53
